00:00:09,410 --> 00:00:14,810
My name is Ava Casper, and today we'll be discussing about CPV manufacturing.

4
00:00:14,810 --> 00:00:19,530
Founded in 1915, CPV is manufactured in Kennon Square, PA.

5
00:00:19,530 --> 00:00:24,690
CPV has been one of the main leaders for high-pressure valves and fittings.

6
00:00:24,690 --> 00:00:28,290
Most of their valves and fittings have been in service for over 30 years.

7
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:34,370
They are made in the USA, and what makes it so cool and unique is you can find some of their valves

8
00:00:34,370 --> 00:00:41,330
and fittings in NASA and in the US Navy. All of their valves are cleaned, tested, and packaged

9
00:00:41,330 --> 00:00:47,970
per CGA and ASTM standards. Now, what makes their design so unique and easy?

10
00:00:48,770 --> 00:00:54,290
Each design has been approved by an oxygen surge tester. Their design features an

11
00:00:54,290 --> 00:01:00,370
ergonomic handle, which makes it extremely easy to turn under high pressures. Now, talking about

12
00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:09,090
high pressures, their highest working pressure for inert gas is 7,800 PSI and 6,000 PSI for oxygen.

13
00:01:10,050 --> 00:01:14,770
Also, their design has a direct pipe thread connection for O-ring seal and welding.

14
00:01:15,650 --> 00:01:18,850
Now, these are just a few things that make them so unique and valuable.

15
